 "title": "Potential PSU Issues",
 "url": "https://www.tweaktown.com/news/77031/is-your-ps5-making-strange-noise-like-ticking-or-whining-this-why",
 "quote": "It's probably an issue with the onboard Power Supply; the power regulation capacitors that SONY use will physically resonate (vibrate) with the power demand fluctuations of the PS5 system (CPU / GPU, RAM, etc); it's typically related to the frame-rate, what is currently on screen and/or multiplayer / network activity."
 },
 {
 "title": "DIY Repair Risks",
 "url": "https://www.avforums.com/threads/coil-whine.2432491/",
 "quote": "It'll be interesting to see how this develops, and I'm curious how many gamers have PS5s with coil whine. I would be very wary of attempting any DIY fixes as the PS5's internal PSU contains high voltage parts which can hold enough charge to kill you, even when the PS5 has been switched off and disconnected from the mains electricity supply."
 },
 {
 "title": "Potential for Defective Unit",
 "url": "https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2020/11/ps5_coil_whine_becomes_a_concern_for_some_early_adopters",
 "quote": "It's difficult to say as your PS5 could be genuinely defective, i.e. it might not be the usual PSU power regulator whine / hiss / sizzle noise that you're hearing."
 }
